      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T09:46:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "[1] This seems to mean that if `SharedFenceDXGISharedHandle` is not available, then we have no possible synchronization for EndAccess? This seems to be breaking the API contracts because then something \"magic\" outside the call to EndAccess needs to handle synchronization. Is it in that case that we\u0027ll have Chromium use the same D3D11 device always? How could we ensure that at the API level?\n\nFor example adding a \"useless\" SharedFenceImplicitD3D11Synchronization. Geoff WDYT?",
      "revId": "824d1caf43dfef3ec030d2f9664ce858bce4067f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
