      "writtenOn": "2025-03-17T10:03:27Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There are two types of D3D synchronizations:\n- fences.\n- keyed mutexes.\n\nKeyed mutexes are already handled by Dawn automatically when clients use it to create shared textures. i.e. Dawn will:\n- Acquire keyed mutexes before accessing the textures in a command buffer [1].\n- Release keyed mutexes just before submitting the command buffer to the driver [2].\n\nWithout fences, the synchronizations should already work if the clients create shared textures with keyed mutexes. Since fences cannot be imported in this case though. We already have a validation that rejects if fences are not supported.\n\n[1] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/d3d11/TextureD3D11.cpp;drc\u003d533610f3b0cddaf48453f570591a39acc7b8042a;l\u003d442\n[2] https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/native/d3d11/QueueD3D11.cpp;drc\u003d75c5e5c6fb11f2e9785b93c142f73996d9169d2d;l\u003d192",
      "parentUuid": "4a550065_5e52c5e0",
      "revId": "824d1caf43dfef3ec030d2f9664ce858bce4067f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
